/-!
# Equations of the Frobenius fixed scheme

Source: latest Weil conjectures blueprint, sec-trace-formula, sk-lem-tf-fixed-points,
`det-tf-fixed-point-equations.md` and its proof
(blueprint: det-tf-fixed-point-equations).

The presentation is recorded by an algebra equivalence and an affine-model isomorphism.
The quotient map is characterized on every polynomial, its kernel is the coordinate
power ideal in B, and the spectrum isomorphism respects the fixed-scheme inclusion.
The last clause gives the same descriptions on every smaller presented model affine,
with the commuting restriction square on spectra.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace WeilConjectures.FiniteFieldDatum.FrobeniusAffineEqualizer

/-- The equations of Fix(Φ^m) in any finite polynomial presentation, including their
compatibility with restriction to every smaller model affine open.
Source: latest blueprint, det-tf-fixed-point-equations.md, both displays and final sentence
(blueprint: det-tf-fixed-point-equations).

Proof: apply `presentation` with the single affine chart given by `j.hom`.
The tensor formula for Frobenius is a ⊗ c ↦ a^(q^m) ⊗ c. The graph-diagonal pullback
is canonically its equalizer, so it is Spec of the tensor algebra
modulo the ideal generated by all φ(b)-b. Transport by the polynomial base-change
identification θ. Each coordinate power difference is one of these generators.
Conversely, modulo the coordinate power differences, the Frobenius substitution and
identity agree on coordinates and scalars; polynomial universality makes them equal.
Thus their difference ideal is precisely the image of `powerIdeal` in B. The composite
polynomial quotient has kernel the sum of the relation and power ideals. It descends
to π on B with exactly the stated kernel, and gives the displayed spectrum isomorphism
over X. For each smaller model affine apply the same computation, obtaining θ', π'
and e'. Naturality of tensor Frobenius makes the scalar-extended restriction map descend
to ρ. Its formula on tensors determines it, since θ and π are surjective. The two sides
of the final square represent the same fixed maps into the smaller affine, so the
equalizer universal property makes them equal. No reduction of the rings is performed. -/
theorem fixedPointEquations (D : FiniteFieldDatum.{u})
    (X₀ : Over (Spec (.of D.k₀))) [LocallyOfFiniteType X₀.hom] [QuasiCompact X₀.hom]
    (A : CommAlgCat.{u} D.k₀) (j : model D A ≅ X₀)
    (r : ℕ) (a : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k₀))
    (p : (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k₀ ⧸ a) ≃ₐ[D.k₀] A) (m : ℕ) (_hm : 1 ≤ m) :
    ∃ h : D.geometricFiber X₀ ⟶ D.geometricFiber X₀,
      h.left = (End.of (D.relativeFrobenius X₀)) ^ m ∧
      ∃ θ : (A ⊗[D.k₀] D.k) ≃+* (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k ⧸ extendedIdeal D r a),
        (∀ f : MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k₀, ∀ c : D.k,
          θ (p (Ideal.Quotient.mk a f) ⊗ₜ c) =
            Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r a)
              (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap D.k₀ D.k) f * MvPolynomial.C c)) ∧
        ∃ π : (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k ⧸ extendedIdeal D r a) →+*
            (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k ⧸ (extendedIdeal D r a ⊔ powerIdeal D m r)),
          (∀ f : MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k,
            π (Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r a) f) =
              Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r a ⊔ powerIdeal D m r) f) ∧
          RingHom.ker π = (powerIdeal D m r).map
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r a)) ∧
          ∃ e : equalizer h.left (𝟙 (D.geometricFiber X₀).left) ≅
              Spec (.of (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k ⧸
                (extendedIdeal D r a ⊔ powerIdeal D m r))),
            e.hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom π) ≫
                Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom θ.toRingHom) ≫ chartMap D X₀ A j.hom =
              equalizer.ι h.left (𝟙 (D.geometricFiber X₀).left) ∧
            ∀ (A' : CommAlgCat.{u} D.k₀) (j' : model D A' ⟶ X₀) (f : A →ₐ[D.k₀] A'),
              IsOpenImmersion j'.left →
              Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom f.toRingHom) ≫ j.hom.left = j'.left →
              ∀ (r' : ℕ) (a' : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k₀))
                (p' : (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k₀ ⧸ a') ≃ₐ[D.k₀] A'),
              ∃ θ' : (A' ⊗[D.k₀] D.k) ≃+*
                  (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k ⧸ extendedIdeal D r' a'),
                (∀ g : MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k₀, ∀ c : D.k,
                  θ' (p' (Ideal.Quotient.mk a' g) ⊗ₜ c) =
                    Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r' a')
                      (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap D.k₀ D.k) g * MvPolynomial.C c)) ∧
                ∃ π' : (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k ⧸ extendedIdeal D r' a') →+*
                    (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k ⧸
                      (extendedIdeal D r' a' ⊔ powerIdeal D m r')),
                  (∀ g : MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k,
                    π' (Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r' a') g) =
                      Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r' a' ⊔ powerIdeal D m r') g) ∧
                  RingHom.ker π' = (powerIdeal D m r').map
                    (Ideal.Quotient.mk (extendedIdeal D r' a')) ∧
                  ∃ e' : pullback
                      (equalizer.ι h.left (𝟙 (D.geometricFiber X₀).left))
                      (chartMap D X₀ A' j') ≅
                      Spec (.of (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k ⧸
                        (extendedIdeal D r' a' ⊔ powerIdeal D m r'))),
                    e'.hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom π') ≫
                        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom θ'.toRingHom) =
                      pullback.snd
                        (equalizer.ι h.left (𝟙 (D.geometricFiber X₀).left))
                        (chartMap D X₀ A' j') ∧
                    ∃ ρ : (MvPolynomial (Fin r) D.k ⧸
                        (extendedIdeal D r a ⊔ powerIdeal D m r)) →+*
                        (MvPolynomial (Fin r') D.k ⧸
                          (extendedIdeal D r' a' ⊔ powerIdeal D m r')),
                      (∀ b : A ⊗[D.k₀] D.k,
                        ρ (π (θ b)) = π' (θ'
                          (Algebra.TensorProduct.map f (AlgHom.id D.k₀ D.k) b))) ∧
                      pullback.fst
                          (equalizer.ι h.left (𝟙 (D.geometricFiber X₀).left))
                          (chartMap D X₀ A' j') ≫ e.hom =
                        e'.hom ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ρ) := by
  sorry

end WeilConjectures.FiniteFieldDatum.FrobeniusAffineEqualizer
